# Build context of the self-hosted image (packaging/docker/Dockerfile): an
# allow-list. Only what the image needs goes in; everything else stays out.
#
# The image ships no content (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-15-self-hosting-design.md,
# sections 4.2 and 8.1): no channel list, no built-in channels, no playlist
# address, no cookies, no keys. tools/selfhost_content_check.py checks the built
# image in CI, and tests/test_selfhost_image.py checks these rules on every run.
*
!LICENSE
!server/
!packaging/help/
!packaging/docker/NOTICE

# Inside the allow-list, still never:
server/builtin_channels.py
**/channels.txt
**/channels.txt.*
**/*.m3u
**/*.m3u8
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.local
**/.DS_Store
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/token
**/relay-key
**/wifi-key
**/setup-code
**/cookies*.txt
**/cstone.json
**/youtube-node.json
**/*.db
**/*.db-*
**/av_private_config.h
